2186127821 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cb1ba97b-634b-5ab2-924d-cc9550d29b5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127822 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127822 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127822 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d26cbbb3-365a-5044-b527-135d62972fe3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127823 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127823 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127823 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2f50ff08-d5af-50c7-b86a-03fd63f3058b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127824 #edb/ref 1080 "DNE" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127824 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127824 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "496462e6-999a-5292-869e-3d711ab01d07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128928 #edb/ref 1069 "e-49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128928 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 2} \\sqrt{x-2}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128928 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "57abae04-4bc2-5fb4-a5b0-5c0c6c85f955" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128928 #edb/ref 1074 "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)= \\sqrt{x-2}\n$$\n\n. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(2) &= \\sqrt{2 - 2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{0} \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the graph of $y=f(x)$ \"starts\" at $x=2$. Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$ as follows:\n\n![](images/a4/a4a64caff7a8b69454ffc8b93a1baad18bf3d93093b3c85a7c4fc3cb9762a2b4.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we notice that the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 2^-} f(x) = \\textrm{DNE}\n$$\n\nwhile the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 2^+} f(x) = 0\n$$\n\nSince the two limits are not equal, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 2} f(x)= \\textrm{DNE}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128929 #edb/ref 1069 "e-50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128929 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\lim_\\limits{x \\rightarrow -\\infty} \\sqrt{3-x}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128929 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1b850386-4730-512a-8408-932f7b6931b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128929 #edb/ref 1074 "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)= \\sqrt{3-x}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$:\n\n![](images/d3/d3960d69c67ce1dbf731975ec1058f590ae6cfd61a3c3b04cb5632ce2eaf68aa.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ decreases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to -\\infty} f(x)= \\infty\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128932 #edb/ref 1069 "e-51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128932 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to -3} \\sqrt[3]{3x-2x^2}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128932 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fbac92a0-de6c-556a-8bf1-030401a5df36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128932 #edb/ref 1074 "We substitute $x=-3$ into the expression, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → - 3)\\sqrt[3]{3x - 2x^{2}} &= \\sqrt[3]{3(-3) - 2(-3)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt[3]{-9 - 18} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt[3]{-27} \\\\\n&=-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129023 #edb/ref 1069 "e-780" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129023 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\infty} \\sqrt[3]{x-1}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129023 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "97cc7a63-900d-52e8-ad0b-2232309d6335" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129023 #edb/ref 1074 "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)= \\sqrt[3]{x-1}\n$$\n\nLet's sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$:\n\n![](images/04/0481bb8a4e6058d3cc41069a210f7fc964d861c7071541432aa7422349410431.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ increases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\infty} f(x)= \\infty\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129195 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129195 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129195 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129195 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129195 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/re